      "title": "The Famine Forecast Lost: Cereal Production Is 1.5x Higher Than In 1972",
      "hook": "The 1970s famine forecast aged badly.",
      "says": [
        "In 1985, progression to secondary school (%) was 77.8. By 2017, it reached 91.3 — 1.2 times higher. Quietly, school kept moving.",
        "In 1972, cereal production was 1083.7 million metric tons. By 2024, it reached 1644.1 million metric tons — 1.5 times higher.",
        "China leads at 5.2 million square kilometers of farmland, then the United States at 4.2 million, Australia at 3.6 million, Brazil at 2.4 million, and Russia at 2.2 million."
      ],
      "closing": "The famine everyone predicted never showed up. It quietly skipped town while the world grew more food.",
      "question": "Which shift matters more: school, grain, or land?"
